<onlyinclude>{{AbilityU10.3
| name        = Lull
| gameimage   = Lull130xWhite.png
| cardimage   = LullModx256.png
| hotkey      = 2
| energy      = 50
| description = A calming wave slows enemies until they fall into a slumber. Enemies woken by damage will be confused and disoriented. Short-term amnesia means all waking enemies forget anything that happened before the lull.
| range       = 10 / 15 / 20 / 25 m
| duration    = 2 / 3 / 4 / 5 s (wave duration)<br> 10 / 13 / 18 / 20 s (sleep duration)
| misc        = 0.80% (Restraint erosion per enemy lulled)<br/>+100% (finisher damage vulnerability)<br/>alertness reset
| subsumable  = true
| cardonly    = {{{1|}}}
| info        = 
*Baruuk expends {{Stat|Ability Efficiency|icon=only}}'''50''' [[energy]] to cast a calming wave over an area of {{Stat|Ability Range|icon=only}}'''10 / 15 / 20 / 25''' meters that lingers for {{Stat|Ability Duration|icon=only}}'''2 / 3 / 4 / 5 ''' seconds. Enemies in sight or aware of Baruuk's presence that enter the area will gradually slow and then enter {{D|Sleep}} for {{Stat|Ability Duration|icon=only}}'''10 / 13 / 18 / 20''' seconds. Sleeping enemies have '''+100%''' [[Damage Vulnerability]] to {{D|Finisher}} damage, but awaken early when damaged, suffering disorientation for a brief moment, along with amnesia causing their [[Stealth#Alertness|alertness]] level to reset.
**Sleeping enemies are open to [[Melee#Finishers|melee finishers]].
**Enemies that awaken early from damage, while still inside the Lull field, will be put back to sleep.
*Cannot be recast while Lull field is active.
*Casting Lull is a full-body animation that stops Baruuk's grounded movement and other actions.
| helminth =
*Subsuming Baruuk to the [[Helminth]] will offer Lull and its augments to be used by other Warframes.
| synergies = 
**Baruuk's [[Baruuk/Abilities#Passive|Restraint]] erodes by <u>'''0.80%'''</u> for each enemy affected.
**Damage dealt by {{A|Desolate Hands}} daggers does '''not''' awaken sleeping enemies.
|augment      =
[[File:EndlessLullabyMod.png|200px|left]]
{{main|Endless Lullaby}}
{{#lst:Endless Lullaby|intro}}
